#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:6
msgid "C Preprocessor vs. Rust Macros"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:8
msgid ""
"The fundamental difference between C-style preprocessor macros and Rust "
"macros lies in **where they hook into compilation**:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:11
msgid "C Preprocessor Macros"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:13
msgid "Hook into the **Tokenizing** step."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:14
msgid ""
"Cannot inspect tokens in detail, but can rearrange and duplicate them (and "
"sometimes append them)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:16
msgid "Can create syntactically invalid output."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:17
msgid ""
"Lack scoping and hygiene, so constructing robust abstractions is difficult."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:19
msgid "Rust Macros"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:21
msgid "Hook into the **Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)** generation step."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:22
msgid "Operate on structured **Token Trees** rather than raw text."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:23
msgid "Must emit valid Rust syntax."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:24
msgid "Maintain **partial hygiene** to prevent accidental name collisions."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:28
msgid ""
"Explain that C macros must guess unused identifiers for internal use, and "
"can access variables not mentioned in their arguments."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:30
msgid ""
"Emphasize that C preprocessor macros don't have access to information from "
"later in compilation, i.e. C syntax or types; they are basically dumb copy-"
"paste."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:33
msgid ""
"To provide better error reporting, the C Preprocessor is actually integrated "
"into the Clang and GCC compilers, but its semantics also constrain it to be "
"usable as a separate pass, so this integration can't be used to improve the "
"behavior of C macros."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:37
msgid ""
"Contrast this with Rust, where macro expansion is inherently part of the "
"compilation process. This lets Rust macros work structurally."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro/cpp-vs-rust-macros.md:39
msgid ""
"Introduce the concept of \"partial hygiene,\" explaining that local variable "
"bindings inside Rust macros do not bleed out into the surrounding code (and "
"vice versa) by default."
msgstr ""
